@@section 1
@@title SQ-CDW Creative Delight worldgen gated on its mods, 2026-11-06 ([creative_delight.md](../creative_delight.md) 24.4, TODO `creativedelight/framework #13`)
@@phase worldgen
@@date 2026-11-06
@@jars creativecommon creativedelight powergrid
@@sources feature_writeup/creative_delight.md
@@text
@@text Not run. Built 2026-11-06, not installed (`development/creativeDelight/build/libs/creativedelight-1.1.0.jar`, with
@@text `packs/worldgen/<mod>/` in it). Every boot needs a new level-name (worldgen registries and biome modifiers are read at
@@text world creation). Mods CDW-01 removes: `myrtrees` and `fruitsdelight` (their packs go off), then the `endersdelight` jar
@@text (no pack goes off: `enders_additions` registers the `endersdelight:` blocks itself). Nested members cannot be removed
@@text (a `[members]` switch only skips script rows, the mod stays loaded), so their packs are always on in the pack.
@@text
@@table
## SQ-CDW-01 | myrtrees removed: no datapack error, level created, wild crop packs line lists it under off
@group B
@commands Rerun after 2026-11-14 (framework #16, plan_bugfix_1114.md 5.1): `prep_srv.sh` now drops the dev-only `srv/kubejs/data/creativedelight/worldgen` source tree (the jar's split copies stay), so check `ls srv/kubejs/data/creativedelight/` has no `worldgen` first. One boot per optional mod, myrtrees first: remove the jar from `mods/`, new level, boot; grep `latest.log` for `Failed to validate datapack`, `Unknown registry key`, `wild crop worldgen packs on`
@pass no datapack error, the level is created; the packs line lists that mod under `off` (endersdelight has no pack of its own, so nothing is listed for it; run r1114)
@fails the error names a `creativedelight:wild/*` file: its rule in `wild_crops.json` lacks `"requires"` and the build guard missed it (`splitWorldgen` namespace regex); error names a pack id `creativedelight:worldgen/<mod>`: that pack's mcmeta
@jars creativedelight powergrid
@from batches/r1115/p1_cdw1.qb
bootexpect Done \(
bootreject ^(?!.*json id corn_delight:).*(Failed to validate datapack|Unknown registry key|Errors in currently selected datapacks)
bootexpect \[creativedelight\] wild crop worldgen packs on: \[.*\]; off \(mod not loaded\): \[[^]]*myrtrees[^]]*\]
shell grep -h "wild crop worldgen packs" logs/latest.log | cut -c1-300
shell test "$(ls mods | grep -c '^myrtrees')" = 0 && echo "jar gone"
shell ls kubejs/data/creativedelight/
look the level is created (Done); no worldgen dir in srv kubejs/data/creativedelight; the packs line as expected

## SQ-CDW-02 | all mods present: wild crop packs line off none, no skip line; rubber trees near a jungle
@group B
@commands All mods present, new level: the packs line, then `/locate biome minecraft:jungle`, tp, forceload a 10x10 chunk box, count `myrtrees:rubberwood_log`
@pass packs line `on: [delightful, enders_additions, ends_delight, farmersdelight, fruitsdelight, fungidelight, hearthandharvest, myrtrees, oceanic_delight]`, `off: none`; `[wild-crops]` counts as SQ-WCD-01 with no `mod not loaded, skipped` line; rubber logs in about 1 chunk in 4
@fails packs missing from the line: `CompartmentPacks.addWorldgen` did not find `packs/worldgen` in the jar (check the jar listing); rubber trees 0 but no skip line: the placed feature did not reach the level (pack added only on `SERVER_DATA`)
@jars creativedelight powergrid
@from batches/r1115/p4_b1.qb
@reviewed 2026-11-16
bootexpect \[creativedelight\] wild crop worldgen packs on: \[.*\]; off \(mod not loaded\): none
kjsreject \[wild-crops\].*mod not loaded, skipped
shell grep -h "wild crop worldgen packs" logs/latest.log | cut -c1-300
shell grep -h "\[wild-crops\]" logs/kubejs/server.log | cut -c1-200 | head -6
> locate biome minecraft:jungle
waitlog nearest minecraft:jungle is at|Could not find 300
capture JG minecraft:jungle is at \[(-?\d+), (~|-?\d+), (-?\d+)\]

> forceload add {JG1-24} {JG3-24} {JG1+23} {JG3+23}
sleep 90
> cdevtest count {JG1-24} 50 {JG3-24} {JG1+23} 160 {JG3+23} myrtrees:rubberwood_log
waitlog verb=count (block=myrtrees:rubberwood_log n=|error=) 600
> cdevtest count {JG1-24} 50 {JG3-24} {JG1+23} 160 {JG3+23} minecraft:jungle_log
waitlog verb=count (block=minecraft:jungle_log n=|error=) 600
expect verb=count block=myrtrees:rubberwood_log n=[1-9]
reject \[cdevtest\] .*done=0
> forceload remove {JG1-24} {JG3-24} {JG1+23} {JG3+23}
look packs line lists delightful, enders_additions, ends_delight, farmersdelight, fruitsdelight, fungidelight, hearthandharvest, myrtrees, oceanic_delight (a newer jar may add packs); rubberwood logs in about 1 chunk in 4 of the 10x10 box (log count / about 5 logs a tree).

## SQ-CDW-03 | [wild-crops] skip lines name only the removed mod's rules
@group B
@commands after each CDW-01 boot, grep `latest.log` for `[wild-crops] mod not loaded, skipped`
@pass exactly the rules of the removed mod (myrtrees: `rubber: needs myrtrees`; fruitsdelight: `hamimelon: needs fruitsdelight`; endersdelight jar: none), nothing else
@fails extra lines: another rule's feature id names the absent mod's namespace without `requires`
@jars creativedelight powergrid
@from batches/r1113/c3_cdw1.qb
shell grep -h "\[wild-crops\] mod not loaded, skipped" logs/kubejs/server.log | cut -c1-200
shell test "$(grep -c "\[wild-crops\] mod not loaded, skipped" logs/kubejs/server.log)" = 1
shell grep -q "\[wild-crops\] mod not loaded, skipped rubber: needs myrtrees" logs/kubejs/server.log
look exactly the one line `rubber: needs myrtrees`; other [wild-flowers] / mob spawn skip lines naming myrtrees are not this row's (judge them: another rule naming the absent namespace without `requires`)

## SQ-CDW-03b | (rerun 5.2) fruitsdelight removed: its 17 rules skip quietly through requires; no skip line names a fruitsdelight feature; apple rule runs
@group B
@commands Rerun after 2026-11-14 (framework #17, plan_bugfix_1114.md 5.1: `"requires": "fruitsdelight"` on the 16 Fruits Delight tree and bush rules of `wild_crops.json`): the CDW-01 boot without fruitsdelight; `grep -c "\[wild-crops\] mod not loaded, skipped" logs/latest.log`; `grep "\[wild-crops\].*fruitsdelight" logs/latest.log`
@pass no `mod not loaded` WARN naming a fruitsdelight feature; the 17 fruitsdelight rules (hamimelon and the 16) skipped quietly through `requires` (their `needs fruitsdelight` lines only); the apple rule (Vinery feature) still runs
@fails a fruitsdelight rule without `requires`: `grep -n fruitsdelight kubejs/data/creativedelight/kubejs/_worldgen/wild_crops.json`; `_biome_rules.js` `requires` handling
@jars creativedelight powergrid
@from batches/r1115/p7_d_fruitsdelight.qb
shell echo "skip lines $(grep -c '\[wild-crops\] mod not loaded, skipped' logs/kubejs/server.log), needs-fruitsdelight $(grep -c '\[wild-crops\] mod not loaded, skipped .*: needs fruitsdelight' logs/kubejs/server.log), naming a fruitsdelight feature $(grep -c '\[wild-crops\] mod not loaded, skipped .*: fruitsdelight:' logs/kubejs/server.log)"
shell test "$(grep -c '\[wild-crops\] mod not loaded, skipped .*: fruitsdelight:' logs/kubejs/server.log)" = 0
shell test "$(grep -c '\[wild-crops\] mod not loaded, skipped .*: needs fruitsdelight' logs/kubejs/server.log)" = 17
shell grep -h "\[wild-crops\] mod not loaded, skipped" logs/kubejs/server.log | grep -i apple | head -3; true
look 17 "<rule>: needs fruitsdelight" lines, none naming a fruitsdelight: feature; no apple skip line

